In this project, I implemented a Binary Tree using C++.
* Created tree nodes dynamically using pointers.
* Built a binary tree structure by connecting parent and child nodes.
* Implemented Preorder traversal to visit nodes in root-left-right order.
* Implemented Inorder traversal to visit nodes in left-root-right order.
* Implemented Postorder traversal to visit nodes in left-right-root order.
* Displayed the tree elements using different traversal techniques.
* Used recursive functions to perform tree operations efficiently.
* Implemented tree deletion to free allocated memory and avoid memory leaks.
* Tested the tree structure and traversal outputs for correctness.
This project helped me understand binary tree creation, tree traversal methods, recursion, dynamic memory allocation, and tree data structure concepts in C++.
